    "legal_toc_section_gYznx3": {
      "type": "legal-toc-section",
      "blocks": {
        "content_section_GLa7AN": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Introduction",
            "title": "1. Introduction and scope",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>This policy explains what we collect about you, why we need it, who helps us process it, and how you stay in control.</strong></p><p>KARMICA BV (“KARMICARE”, “we”, “us” or “our”) respects your fundamental right to privacy and is committed to protecting your personal data in full compliance with:</p><ul><li>The <strong>General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679</strong> (“GDPR”);</li><li>The <strong>Belgian Data Protection Act of 30 July 2018;</strong></li><li>The <strong>Belgian Electronic Communications Act of 13 June 2005</strong>, transposing the ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC as amended;</li><li>Applicable international privacy legislation, including the <strong>UK GDPR</strong> and the <strong>California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA)</strong> as amended by the <strong>California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA)</strong>.</li></ul><p>This policy explains how we collect, process, store, disclose and safeguard your personal data when you visit our website, order from us, start a plan or contact our customer care.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_g6nYeY": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Who we are",
            "title": "2. Safety and standards",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>KARMICA BV in Bruges is responsible for your personal data. Every privacy question goes to one address: </strong><a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a><strong>.</strong></p><p>The data controller responsible for the processing of your personal data is:</p><p><strong>KARMICA BV,</strong> Vizierstraat 28, 8000 Bruges, Belgium · Company and VAT number BE 0676.972.896 · Register of Legal Persons: Enterprise Court of Ghent, division Bruges · <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a></p><p>For all questions, privacy requests or to exercise your rights under the GDPR, write to our Data Privacy Lead at <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_iDEfUH": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Data we process",
            "title": "3. Refunds, withdrawal and the 60-day guarantee",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Changed your mind about a one-time order? You have 14 days. On the 60-Day plan or the Karmicare Year, you have 60 days to live the ritual and still get a full refund.</strong></p><p><strong>3.1 Refund timelines by purchase type</strong></p><p><strong>One-time orders (Try once): your legal right</strong></p><ul><li>You have a statutory right of withdrawal of 14 calendar days from the date of physical delivery (Article VI.47 of the Belgian Code of Economic Law).</li><li>If you withdraw within this period, we reimburse all payments received from you, including standard delivery charges, within 14 calendar days of receiving the returned unopened goods or proof of return.</li><li>Refunds are issued via the same payment method you used for the purchase.</li></ul><p><strong>60-Day plan and Karmicare Year: Karmicare promise</strong></p><ul><li>KARMICARE gives you an extended commercial 60-calendar-day satisfaction guarantee.</li><li>Building a biorhythmic ritual takes consistent daily practice, so you have 60 calendar days from delivery to experience and evaluate Awake and Asleep.</li><li>Not completely satisfied? Email <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a> within 60 calendar days of delivery and we refund 100% of your plan order to your original payment method.</li></ul><p><strong>3.2 Packaging notice: airless pump and first-use priming</strong></p><ul><li>Hermetic airless protection. Our formulas are housed in hygienic airless pump dispensers that shield the active formulation from air, oxidation and microbial contamination without relying on harsh preservatives.</li><li>Unprimed factory state. Our airless bottles are not pre-pumped. When you unbox them, the internal vacuum chamber is sealed and completely dry.</li><li>First-use priming (3 to 10 pumps). On first use, press the pump head firmly 3 to 10 times to activate the piston, clear the air pocket and draw the formula into the nozzle.</li></ul><p><strong>Hygiene seal exemption</strong> (Art. VI.53, 5° WER / Art. 16(e) Directive 2011/83/EU)</p><ul><li>Sealed goods that are not suitable for return for health protection or hygiene reasons, and that were unsealed after delivery, are exempt from the statutory right of withdrawal.</li><li>For one-time orders, an unprimed bottle with intact packaging can be returned within 14 calendar days. Once primed, the bottle is unsealed and opened for intimate personal use, which ends the statutory right of return for one-time orders.</li><li>On the 60-Day plan and the Karmicare Year, the 60-day satisfaction guarantee (section 3.1) still applies after priming.</li></ul><p><strong>3.3 How to request a refund or return</strong></p><ol><li>Email <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a> with your order number and plan type (one-time order, 60-Day plan or Karmicare Year).</li><li>For returns of unopened one-time orders, we send you a return authorisation and the warehouse address: KARMICA BV, Returns Department, Vizierstraat 28, 8000 Bruges, Belgium.</li><li>Return shipping costs for one-time orders are paid by you, unless the item arrived damaged or defective.</li><li>All refunds are issued within 14 calendar days via the same payment method you used at checkout. We never replace a refund with a store voucher unless you explicitly ask for one.</li></ol>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_FcEDdA": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Purposes",
            "title": "4. Two-year legal guarantee of conformity",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>If something is faulty, you are covered for two years from delivery, and the law assumes the fault was there from the start.</strong></p><p>Under Belgian law (Article 1649bis and following of the Civil Code and Book VI WER, implementing Directive (EU) 2019/771), European consumers benefit from a mandatory<strong> two-year legal guarantee of conformity</strong> on all goods purchased from KARMICARE.</p><p><strong>4.1 Two-year presumption of conformity</strong></p><ul><li>If a delivered item is defective, non-conforming or damaged on delivery, you are protected for two full years (24 months) from the date of delivery.</li><li>Any defect that appears within those two years is presumed to have existed at the time of delivery, unless proven otherwise or incompatible with the nature of the goods.</li></ul><p><strong>4.2 Your remedies</strong></p><ol><li>Free replacement or repair. You choose between a free replacement and a repair, provided the remedy you choose is not impossible or disproportionate.</li><li>Price reduction or ending the contract. If replacement is impossible, or cannot be carried out within a reasonable time and without significant inconvenience, you can ask for an appropriate price reduction or a full refund and end the contract.</li></ol><p><strong>4.3 Telling us about a defect</strong></p><p>Let us know within<strong> two months</strong> of discovering a defect (Article 1649quater, §2 of the Belgian Civil Code). Email <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a> with photos or a video of the defect and your order details.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_xKcNPj": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Service providers",
            "title": "5. Delivery and risk in transit",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Until your parcel is in your hands, it is our responsibility.</strong></p><ul><li>Risk in transit (Art. VI.44 WER). The risk of loss, damage or theft in transit stays with KARMICARE until the parcel is handed to you or to the recipient you name.</li><li>Delayed deliveries. If delivery is later than the agreed date (or later than 30 days when no date was agreed), you can ask us to deliver within an additional reasonable period. If we still fail to deliver, you can end the contract and receive a full refund within 14 calendar days.</li></ul><p><strong>Delivery windows</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Belgium and the Netherlands:</strong> 1–3 business days</li><li><strong>European Union and United Kingdom: </strong>2–5 business days</li><li><strong>United States and Canada:</strong> 4–8 business days</li><li><strong>Australia and rest of world:</strong> 6–12 business days</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_rnPj6g": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Transfers",
            "title": "6. Your plan: freedom to pause, skip or cancel",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>No lock-in. Pause, skip or cancel whenever you like, and we email you before every renewal charge.</strong></p><ul><li>No lock-in. There is no minimum commitment period.</li><li>60-day satisfaction guarantee. On the 60-Day plan or the Karmicare Year, you have 60 calendar days from delivery to ask for a refund, paid back to your original payment method.</li><li>Full control. Pause, skip a delivery, adjust your billing frequency (for example every 30, 60 or 90 days), change your shipping address or cancel at any time in your <a href=\"https://checkout.karmicare.com/a/loop_subscriptions/customer\" target=\"_blank\">customer portal</a>.</li><li>Renewal reminders. We email you before every scheduled renewal charge, so you have time to review, change or cancel the order before it is processed.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_EAKJLC": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Retention",
            "title": "7. Pricing transparency",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>The price you see includes VAT. A “was” price is always our lowest price of the previous 30 days, and every review comes from a verified order.</strong></p><p>In accordance with the EU Omnibus Directive (2019/2161) and the Belgian Code of Economic Law (Art. VI.19/1 WER):</p><ul><li><strong>All-inclusive pricing.</strong> Prices shown to European consumers include VAT and all applicable levies. Shipping costs are shown before final checkout.</li><li><strong>Genuine discounts.</strong> When we announce a price reduction, the reference price is the lowest price KARMICARE applied in the preceding 30 days.</li><li><strong>Authentic reviews. </strong>We only collect and publish reviews from verified purchasers. Reviews are never manipulated, selectively hidden or bought.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_dGmgBJ": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Your rights",
            "title": "8. Complaints and dispute resolution",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Write to us first: we acknowledge every complaint within 24 hours and commit to resolving it within 7 business days. If we cannot agree, independent help is available.</strong></p><p>Email <a href=\"mailto:care@karmicare.com\" target=\"_blank\">care@karmicare.com</a> about any issue with an order, a delivery or a formula. If we cannot reach an amicable solution, you have access to independent out-of-court dispute resolution.<br/><br/><strong>8.1 Belgian Consumer Mediation Service</strong></p><p>For Belgian and cross-border European disputes: Consumer Mediation Service (Consumentenombudsdienst / Service de Médiation pour le Consommateur), North Gate II, Boulevard du Roi Albert II 8, box 1, 1000 Brussels, Belgium · Tel. +32 2 702 52 00 · <a href=\"mailto:contact@consumentenombudsdienst.be\" target=\"_blank\">contact@consumentenombudsdienst.be</a> · <a href=\"https://consumerombudsman.be/en\" target=\"_blank\">consumerombudsman.be/en</a></p><p><strong>8.2 European Consumer Centre</strong></p><p>For a dispute across EU borders, the European Consumer Centre in your country can help. In Belgium: European Consumer Centre Belgium, Koning Albert II-laan 16, 1000 Brussels · Tel. +32 2 277 99 00 · <a href=\"mailto:info@eccbelgium.be\" target=\"_blank\">info@eccbelgium.be</a> · <a href=\"https://www.eccbe.eu\" target=\"_blank\">eccbe.eu</a></p><p>The EU Online Dispute Resolution (ODR) platform closed on 20 July 2025, so it is no longer a route for complaints.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_section_CDtWCV": {
          "type": "content_section",
          "settings": {
            "nav_label": "Cookies",
            "title": "9. Applicable law and jurisdiction",
            "lead": "",
            "content": "<p><strong>Belgian law applies, but never at the expense of the protection your own country gives you.</strong></p><p>Contracts concluded with KARMICARE are governed by Belgian law. Under <strong>Article 6 of the Rome I Regulation</strong> (EC) No 593/2008, consumers residing in the European Union or the UK also keep the mandatory protection of the consumer laws of their country of habitual residence.<br/><br/>Under <strong>Article 18 of the Brussels I bis Regulation</strong> (EU) No 1215/2012, you can bring a claim before the competent courts of the place where you live.</p>"
          }
        },
